# high-value-lot-escort-authoritative-valuation-source

For high-value escort threshold ($500K per SEC-HV-01), use the current LMI artifact value — not the Finance team's older estimate. If LMI value exceeds $500,000, continuous escort is mandatory and cannot be waived.

## Procedures
- 1. Locate the lot value in the Lot Move Instruction (LMI) artifact — this is the authoritative current value.
- 2. Compare LMI value against the $500,000 threshold from policy SEC-HV-01.
- 3. If LMI value > $500,000: activate continuous visual escort; the lot must never be left unattended at any point including staging areas and brief stops.
- 4. If Finance or any other source quotes a lower value, check whether it is more recent than the LMI. If it is older or explicitly marked 'pending revision', discard it in favor of the LMI value.
- 5. Arrange an authorized escort (Security Officer or trained handler buddy system) before initiating transport.
- 6. Maintain continuous line-of-sight with the lot for the entire transport and staging duration.

## Conventions
- LMI artifact value is authoritative for escort threshold decisions; Finance estimates are advisory only unless they post-date the LMI.
- A 'pending PO revision' note on a Finance estimate does not lower the current operative value for safety purposes — use the higher, current LMI figure.

